WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.801
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everyone.

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:05.934
You're here, you made it.
Thank you for tuning in.

00:00:05.934 --> 00:00:08.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:11.334
Well, guys, we are coming to you
after President Biden's

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:14.234
very first State of the Union
address.

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:15.434
Yep, it was historic.

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:18.133
400 representatives,
100 senators,

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:20.434
and size 96 font
on the teleprompter.

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:21.868
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, it's amazing.

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:24.767
That's right, Biden was at
the podium with Kamala Harris

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:26.667
and Nancy Pelosi
right behind him.

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:28.434
Fox News was like,
"Throw in Hillary

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:29.734
and you got all Four Horsemen."

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:32.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:36.834
During his speech, Biden
introduced his new unity agenda.

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:39.267
Unity agenda, yeah.
And you can tell it worked

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:42.767
'cause every single Republican
ignored him.

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:44.868
Meanwhile, before his
State of the Union,

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:48.567
Biden had a 30-minute call with
Ukrainian President Zelenskyy.

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:51.167
Yeah, Zelenskyy asked Biden
to share weapons

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:53.634
and Biden asked Zelenskyy
to share his approval rating.

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:55.300
[ Laughter ]
It's a good deal.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.467
At the same time Zelenskyy
and Biden were talking,

00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:00.534
Putin and Trump were on
their own phone call like,

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:03.234
"You think they're
talking about us?

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:06.868
They're totally
talking about us. I know."

00:01:06.868 --> 00:01:10.501
Well, as the war continues,
I read that 12 Russian diplomats

00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:13.634
were expelled from the U.S.
and sent back to Russia

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:15.968
after being accused of spying.

00:01:15.968 --> 00:01:17.400
[ Audience oohs ]

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.634
The U.S. knew they made the
right move when eight Russians

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:22.100
and four office plants got up
and left for the airport.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:27.801
Meanwhile, NASA said that
despite the war,

00:01:27.801 --> 00:01:30.701
U.S. and Russian astronauts
are still working together

00:01:30.701 --> 00:01:32.968
on the
International Space Station.

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:34.434
It's not great though.

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:38.667
Today, one astronaut was like,
"Houston, things are awkward."

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:41.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.033
And finally,
in some lighter news,

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:45.100
today is Mardi Gras, everybody.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:48.334
Yes!

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.868
I love it!

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:56.901
Doing body shots off a stranger
is a sure sign

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:58.901
that things are
getting back to normal.

00:01:58.901 --> 00:02:05.834
[ Laughter ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:08.701
Yep, Mardi Gras, just as the CDC

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:11.167
told us that we could
loosen restrictions.

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:12.634
It's like getting
your driver's license

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:14.234
then entering the Indy 500.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.100
I wish NBC covered Mardi Gras

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.734
like they do
the Thanksgiving Day parade.

00:02:18.734 --> 00:02:20.067
"Let's check in with Al Roker,

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:22.534
who's with a topless grandmother
from Daytona. Al?"

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:24.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:27.000
That's right, Mardi Gras is
a day to drink and celebrate.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.067
It's basically your liver's
dress rehearsal

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:30.367
for St. Patrick's Day.

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:33.200
We have a great show, everybody,
give it up for the Roots!

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.334
Come on!

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:43.968
♪♪

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:53.567
♪♪

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:56.367
Thank you so much. What a fun
show we have for tonight.

00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:58.534
But first, guys, I follow

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:01.667
Chef Jose Andres
on social media.

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:03.868
He, of course,
has this organization,

00:03:03.868 --> 00:03:05.133
World Central Kitchen.

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:07.501
And he goes around,
and when there's a disaster

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:09.033
or people need him, he's there.

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:11.467
He's feeding all these people
who can't get food,

00:03:11.467 --> 00:03:12.934
can't get access to food.

00:03:12.934 --> 00:03:16.033
Right now, he's in Ukraine,
and it's heartbreaking.

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:18.734
But it's also amazing
what he's doing.

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:20.667
He shows up.
He shows up for people.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:24.000
And so any way we can help him
help people we want to.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:25.434
So tonight we thought
we'd shine a light

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:26.734
on World Central Kitchen.

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:30.534
If you can give anything,
go to wck.org.

00:03:30.534 --> 00:03:33.067
A dollar goes a long way.
Anything you can give helps.

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:34.300
Thank you very much.

